request.description:
Gets a list of the distribution cabinets that the API key can see, sorted by name.

If a zone ID is specified, the list has only the distribution cabinets in that zone. Leave out the zone ID, or send 0, to get every distribution cabinet that the API key can see.

An API key with a data access group sees the distribution cabinets in the zones of that group. It also sees the distribution cabinets that have no zone. A distribution cabinet with no zone is listed only when you leave out the zone ID or send 0.

The call returns HTTP 200 with an empty list in these cases:

- no zone has this zone ID;
- the zone is not in the data access group of the API key;
- the zone has no distribution cabinets.

Each distribution cabinet consists of:

- `id`: the unique ID;
- `name`: the name;
- `latitude` and `longitude`: the position on the map. Both are `null` when the cabinet has no position;
- `note`: the note, or `null` when the cabinet has no note;
- `address`: the address, or `null` when the cabinet has no address yet. SmartOLT looks up the address from the position in the background, unless a user typed the address;
- `address_auto`: `1` when SmartOLT fills the address, `0` when a user typed it;
- `address_pending_since`: the time since the cabinet waits for its automatic address, or `null` when it does not wait;
- `external_id`: the unique external ID, or `null` when the cabinet has no external ID;
- `zone_id`: the zone ID, or `null` when the cabinet has no zone;
- `zone_name`: the zone name, or an empty string when the cabinet has no zone.

All values are strings, except the `null` values.

