request.description:
## Open an external ticket on an ONU

Use this call when your own ticket system opens a ticket for the customer of an ONU. SmartOLT shows the ticket on the ONU in the ONU lists and on the ONU page until the ticket is resolved. Only `ticket_number` is required. The other fields are the fields of the SmartOLT ticket form. The ticket shows API as its author. When the request sets an assignee, SmartOLT sends the assignee the ticket assignment email, unless `status` in the same request resolves the ticket.

The call is safe to repeat. When the ONU already has an open external ticket with the same `ticket_number`, SmartOLT does not create a second ticket and does not change the open one. It returns the open ticket with `created` set to `false`. To change that ticket, use [`update_external_ticket`](https://api.smartolt.com/#b617d4e5-ee3e-3164-f4cb-59a4170f5f55).

**Assigning a user.** `assignee_user_id` and `assignee_email` require an API key that meets all of these conditions:

- it is not read-only;
- the **User management** option is enabled on it;
- it has no data access group.

If the request includes `assignee_user_id` or `assignee_email` and the key does not meet these conditions, SmartOLT rejects the whole request with HTTP 403 and `error_code` `forbidden`, and does not create the ticket. To open the ticket without an assignee, leave both fields out.

Responses include `assignee_email` only for a key that meets these conditions. For any other key the field is omitted; `assignee_user_id` is always returned.

A read-only API key cannot use this call. The response is HTTP 403 with `error_code` `forbidden` and the message `Readonly API Key doesn't have rights to make changes.`, and SmartOLT does not create the ticket.

It returns HTTP 400 and does not create the ticket when no ONU was found for the provided ONU external ID, or when a field is not valid. The `error_code` names the problem:

- `invalid_ticket_number`: `ticket_number` is missing, empty or longer than 100 characters;
- `invalid_url`: `url` does not start with http:// or https://, or is longer than 500 characters;
- `invalid_text`: `subject` is longer than 200 characters, or `note` is longer than 5000 characters;
- `invalid_value`: `ticket_type`, `priority` or `status` is not one of the listed values;
- `invalid_schedule`: `scheduled_at` is not in one of the listed formats, `duration` is not a whole number from 5 to 1440, or the request sends `duration` and the ticket has no start;
- `assignee_not_allowed`: no active user with this ID or email can take tickets on this ONU. The user must be able to open the ONU and view tickets. The response does not say whether the user does not exist or cannot take the ticket.

It returns HTTP 409 and does not create the ticket when another request works on the same ticket at the same time:

- `ticket_busy`: another request is opening a ticket with the same number on this ONU and did not finish within 10 seconds. Send the request again;
- `ticket_changed`: another change to the new ticket was saved at the same moment. Send the request again.

It returns HTTP 500 with `error_code` `internal_error` when the database did not save the ticket. SmartOLT saves nothing; send the request again.

