request.description:
## Update an external ticket on an ONU

Changes the external ticket with this `ticket_number` on the ONU. SmartOLT changes only the fields that the request sends; the other fields keep their values. When the ONU has an open external ticket with this number, the call changes that ticket. When it has no open one, the call changes the most recently created resolved external ticket with this number.

A `status` of `new` or `in_progress` reopens a resolved ticket, and the same request can also set its assignee. A `status` of `solved`, `no_solution`, `archived` or `cancelled` resolves the ticket with that status. To resolve a ticket with the status `solved` and change nothing else, you can also use [`resolve_external_ticket`](https://api.smartolt.com/#ea198368-d9b0-e4f8-c7d0-6bb4d93f98f8). When the request sets a new assignee, SmartOLT sends the assignee the ticket assignment email, unless `status` in the same request resolves the ticket. SmartOLT saves all changes of one request together: when the request fails, it saves none of them.

**Assigning a user.** `assignee_user_id` and `assignee_email` require an API key that meets all of these conditions:

- it is not read-only;
- the **User management** option is enabled on it;
- it has no data access group.

If the request includes `assignee_user_id` or `assignee_email` and the key does not meet these conditions, SmartOLT rejects the whole request with HTTP 403 and `error_code` `forbidden`, and does not change the ticket. To change other fields without an assignee, leave both fields out.

Responses include `assignee_email` only for a key that meets these conditions. For any other key the field is omitted; `assignee_user_id` is always returned.

A read-only API key cannot use this call. The response is HTTP 403 with `error_code` `forbidden` and the message `Readonly API Key doesn't have rights to make changes.`, and SmartOLT does not change the ticket.

It returns HTTP 404 with `error_code` `not_found` when the ONU has no external ticket with this number, open or resolved.

It returns HTTP 400 and does not change the ticket when no ONU was found for the provided ONU external ID, or when a field is not valid. The `error_code` names the problem:

- `invalid_ticket_number`: `ticket_number` is missing, empty or longer than 100 characters;
- `invalid_url`: `url` does not start with http:// or https://, or is longer than 500 characters;
- `invalid_text`: `subject` is empty or longer than 200 characters, or `note` is longer than 5000 characters;
- `invalid_ticket_type`: this ticket cannot have the `ticket_type` that the request sends;
- `invalid_value`: `ticket_type`, `priority` or `status` is not one of the listed values;
- `invalid_schedule`: `scheduled_at` is not in one of the listed formats, `duration` is not a whole number from 5 to 1440, or the request sends `duration` and the ticket has no start;
- `assignee_not_allowed`: no active user with this ID or email can take tickets on this ONU. The user must be able to open the ONU and view tickets. The response does not say whether the user does not exist or cannot take the ticket.

It returns HTTP 409 and does not change the ticket in these cases:

- `ticket_resolved`: the ticket is resolved, the request sets a different assignee, and `status` is not `new` or `in_progress`. To reopen the ticket and assign it, send `status` `new` or `in_progress` in the same request;
- `ticket_number_open`: `status` would reopen this resolved ticket, but another external ticket with the same number is open on the ONU. Resolve the open ticket first;
- `ticket_changed`: another change to this ticket was saved at the same moment. Send the request again.

It returns HTTP 500 with `error_code` `internal_error` when the database did not save the changes. SmartOLT saves none of them; send the request again.

